73
00:04:25.246 --> 00:04:26.699
(narrator) The traffic light turns red.

74
00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:35.368
(narrator) The old way: long arms reach from the light into each car's state and set its speed to zero, the cars jolt to a stop, and a chat notice says physics has left the chat.

75
00:04:35.368 --> 00:04:37.756
(narrator) The new way: the light sends a brake envelope.

76
00:04:37.756 --> 00:04:43.622
(narrator) The gas car's card opens Car brake with brake pads; the hybrid's opens HybridCar brake with a battery that fills.

77
00:04:43.622 --> 00:04:46.114
(narrator) The light sees both only as Vehicle silhouettes.

78
00:04:46.114 --> 00:04:53.225
(narrator) Then a card sprouts a getter and a setter for every field and its padlock pops open; it is a struct in a trench coat, and the coat drops.

79
00:04:53.827 --> 00:04:55.587
♪ Red light! The old way: ♪

80
00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:57.687
♪ the light reaches into every car ♪

81
00:04:57.687 --> 00:04:59.707
♪ and sets its speed to zero. (Screech!) ♪

82
00:04:59.707 --> 00:05:01.527
♪ No brake lights. Physics left the chat. ♪

83
00:05:01.527 --> 00:05:03.787
♪ The new way: one message. “Brake!” (Brake!) ♪

84
00:05:03.787 --> 00:05:05.987
♪ A gas car squeezes its brake pads; ♪

85
00:05:05.987 --> 00:05:07.847
♪ a hybrid recharges its battery. ♪

86
00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:09.607
